WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.522
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:19.792 --> 00:20.938
It was you, wasn't it?

3
00:20.938 --> 00:22.314
What do you mean?

4
00:22.314 --> 00:24.626
What do I mean?

5
00:24.626 --> 00:27.319
You mean posting about the blank-round incident on the unit cafe

6
00:27.319 --> 00:30.242
and saying they let you off because you're the division commander's son?

7
00:31.334 --> 00:32.407
So it was you.

8
00:32.407 --> 00:33.534
It wasn't me.

9
00:33.534 --> 00:35.496
You little...

10
00:36.328 --> 00:38.830
Then who was it if not you?

11
00:38.830 --> 00:40.123
Hyeon Uk.

12
00:40.123 --> 00:43.034
I already know. That's why I'm asking.

13
00:44.294 --> 00:46.116
You know that much?

14
00:47.125 --> 00:48.405
What?

15
00:49.049 --> 00:51.051
Then you know the night-watch incident,

16
00:51.051 --> 00:54.513
the blank rounds, even the firing pin retaining pin...

17
00:54.513 --> 00:57.959
I did all of that on purpose?

18
00:57.959 --> 01:00.352
What did you say?

19
01:00.352 --> 01:01.792
You little bastard...

20
01:01.792 --> 01:04.459
Then why don't you know what you did to me?

21
01:04.459 --> 01:06.566
What are you talking about?

22
01:06.566 --> 01:08.500
You don't know why I got sent home from training, do you?

23
01:08.500 --> 01:10.654
Sent home?

24
01:10.654 --> 01:12.364
You...

25
01:12.364 --> 01:14.626
You left because you got hurt.

26
01:14.626 --> 01:18.203
Then you don't know why I got hurt?

27
01:18.203 --> 01:21.918
That was because you got hurt and were sent home...

28
01:21.918 --> 01:24.042
You really don't know, do you?

29
01:24.042 --> 01:26.753
Or are you pretending not to?

30
01:26.753 --> 01:29.673
Of course. Why would the precious division commander's son

31
01:29.673 --> 01:33.746
care what happened to some nobody like me?

32
01:34.459 --> 01:36.596
Hyeon Uk...

33
01:36.596 --> 01:38.834
I think you've got the wrong idea.

34
01:38.834 --> 01:40.147
Wrong idea?

35
01:40.147 --> 01:42.978
You almost crippled me,

36
01:42.978 --> 01:44.610
- and that's a misunderstanding? - No...

37
01:44.610 --> 01:46.440
You ruined a whole year of my life.

38
01:46.440 --> 01:48.859
Wait, Hyeon Uk. Hold on.

39
01:48.859 --> 01:52.671
What on earth are you talking about?

40
01:56.950 --> 01:59.077
If you don't know, listen carefully.

41
01:59.077 --> 02:01.522
I'll tell you exactly what you did to me.

42
02:02.209 --> 02:04.667
Don't you remember individual combat training...

43
02:04.667 --> 02:06.360
at boot camp?

44
02:13.091 --> 02:18.378
[EP05. The Division Commander's Son]

45
02:23.709 --> 02:25.604
Hyeon Uk...

46
02:25.604 --> 02:27.814
I know it's way too late,

47
02:27.814 --> 02:29.656
but I'm really sorry.

48
02:31.209 --> 02:34.062
I really had no idea that happened.

49
02:35.155 --> 02:38.617
Who knows if you didn't know...

50
02:38.617 --> 02:40.420
or just pretended not to?

51
02:43.413 --> 02:44.957
Corporal Park Min Seok.

52
02:44.957 --> 02:46.958
I'll head in first.

53
02:46.958 --> 02:49.336
I have to get up first and move fast.

54
02:49.336 --> 02:52.907
I have to work myself to death to stay in everyone's good graces.

55
02:54.549 --> 02:56.785
Unlike someone important like you.

56
03:06.876 --> 03:09.212
Hyeon Uk...

57
03:28.500 --> 03:29.543
Hey.

58
03:29.543 --> 03:30.585
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

59
03:30.585 --> 03:31.959
Why are you still up?

60
03:31.959 --> 03:32.963
Sorry!

61
03:32.963 --> 03:35.137
- Get inside and go to sleep. - Understood.

62
03:36.925 --> 03:40.357
Good night, Corporal Park Min Seok!

63
03:53.876 --> 03:54.985
Wake up!

64
03:54.985 --> 03:56.167
Hey, Hyeon Uk.

65
03:56.167 --> 03:57.237
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

66
03:57.237 --> 03:58.751
Leave me something to do too.

67
03:58.751 --> 03:59.865
Understood!

68
03:59.865 --> 04:01.185
Thanks.

69
04:07.751 --> 04:08.790
At ease!

70
04:08.790 --> 04:10.959
I still can't shake this hangover.

71
04:10.959 --> 04:12.083
Chungseong! Love you!

72
04:12.083 --> 04:13.968
No need for formal salutes between us.

73
04:13.968 --> 04:16.173
Chungseong! Love you!

74
04:17.124 --> 04:19.125
What brings you here this early?

75
04:19.125 --> 04:20.385
Can't I?

76
04:20.385 --> 04:22.387
I'm visiting my old home.

77
04:22.387 --> 04:25.724
Then come on Lunar New Year or Chuseok too...

78
04:25.724 --> 04:28.680
Hey, Im Da Hye, you've gotten bold!

79
04:29.834 --> 04:32.223
You guys sure are in a good mood.

80
04:32.223 --> 04:34.167
We are.

81
04:34.167 --> 04:36.944
I like seeing you so often.

82
04:36.944 --> 04:37.944
Me too!

83
04:37.944 --> 04:40.352
Ugh, gross.

84
04:40.948 --> 04:42.491
Hey, Park Min Seok.

85
04:42.491 --> 04:44.993
Why aren't you saying anything?

86
04:44.993 --> 04:46.920
I like it too.

87
04:47.876 --> 04:49.247
What?

88
04:49.247 --> 04:50.332
What's with him?

89
04:50.332 --> 04:51.458
Not sure.

90
04:51.458 --> 04:53.667
He's been like this all morning.

91
04:56.250 --> 04:58.089
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

92
04:58.089 --> 05:00.000
You're the future of Barracks One. You know that, right?

93
05:00.000 --> 05:01.635
- Thank you! - Yeah. You're doing great.

94
05:01.635 --> 05:02.886
- Keep it up. - Understood!

95
05:02.886 --> 05:05.096
So wake me up in ten minutes, okay?

96
05:05.096 --> 05:05.959
Understood.

97
05:05.959 --> 05:08.061
Okay.

98
05:13.459 --> 05:16.191
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, here's a pillow...

99
05:16.191 --> 05:18.044
Sorry...

100
05:18.044 --> 05:19.508
You trying to die?

101
05:19.508 --> 05:22.781
Hey, I'm not Sergeant Choi Il Gu anymore.

102
05:22.781 --> 05:24.115
I'm a staff sergeant. Staff sergeant.

103
05:24.115 --> 05:26.243
Watch it. You want to end up in the brig?

104
05:26.243 --> 05:27.834
- Sorry. - You're out of your mind.

105
05:27.834 --> 05:29.920
Rest well!

106
05:34.376 --> 05:36.294
Are you insane? Smoking in here?

107
05:36.294 --> 05:38.365
It's a pen.

108
05:39.506 --> 05:41.334
What? Where's the ink cartridge?

109
05:41.334 --> 05:44.428
This is a pen filter.

110
05:44.428 --> 05:47.514
You take the ink out and suck on the empty tube.

111
05:47.514 --> 05:50.209
Air flows through, so it feels like taking a drag.

112
05:50.209 --> 05:54.011
And if you roll up some tissue and put it inside...

113
05:55.689 --> 05:59.401
it adds resistance, so it feels just like smoking a real cigarette.

114
05:59.401 --> 06:01.542
You do the dumbest things.

115
06:01.542 --> 06:03.432
- Give it here. - Wait...

116
06:04.083 --> 06:06.161
Ugh, it reeks of spit.

117
06:07.751 --> 06:10.292
It really does feel like a cigarette.

118
06:10.292 --> 06:12.447
Pretty amazing, isn't it?

119
06:16.417 --> 06:18.167
- Confiscated. - What?

120
06:18.167 --> 06:19.334
That's mine.

121
06:19.334 --> 06:22.090
Instead of making this thing, work on your enunciation.

122
06:22.090 --> 06:24.250
My diction is basically announcer level.

123
06:24.250 --> 06:27.095
No way. Say, "Company work detail, assemble."

124
06:27.095 --> 06:28.138
Company commander, assemble.

125
06:28.138 --> 06:29.751
Why would the company commander assemble?

126
06:29.751 --> 06:30.766
What? No...

127
06:30.766 --> 06:32.834
- You're just like the command sergeant major. - What?

128
06:32.834 --> 06:34.292
Come on, I'm not that bad.

129
06:34.292 --> 06:36.354
"I'm not that bad."

130
06:36.354 --> 06:38.417
It's mine. Give it back. It smells like spit.

131
06:38.417 --> 06:42.167
"It smells like spit." You smell worse.

132
06:42.167 --> 06:43.709
It hurts.

133
06:43.709 --> 06:45.363
Why does this suddenly hurt when I smoke?

134
06:45.363 --> 06:49.117
By the way, how did you hurt your arm?

135
06:49.117 --> 06:52.000
Something fell on me in the supply warehouse.

136
06:52.000 --> 06:53.876
On purpose...

137
06:53.876 --> 06:54.915
Never mind.

138
06:54.915 --> 06:56.666
- Sung Yoon Mo. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

139
06:56.666 --> 06:59.086
You're my left hand now.

140
06:59.086 --> 07:00.167
I must've heard you wrong.

141
07:00.167 --> 07:02.964
From now on, you do everything my left hand would.

142
07:02.964 --> 07:06.167
- What? - Just do everything I'd normally do.

143
07:06.167 --> 07:07.676
Got it?

144
07:10.472 --> 07:11.932
This is wild.

145
07:11.932 --> 07:14.250
It really feels like a cigarette!

146
07:14.250 --> 07:17.103
Guess it really is almost time for us to go home.

147
07:17.103 --> 07:20.405
How is nobody even hanging around the smoking area?

148
07:24.945 --> 07:26.446
Chungseong! Love you!

149
07:26.446 --> 07:28.292
Here to smoke?

150
07:28.292 --> 07:30.959
My body just brought me here.

151
07:30.959 --> 07:33.042
My head says quit,

152
07:33.042 --> 07:34.865
but my heart's here...

153
07:36.122 --> 07:37.958
But what brings you two here?

154
07:37.958 --> 07:39.292
What?

155
07:39.292 --> 07:40.918
Uh... well...

156
07:40.918 --> 07:42.045
- Huh? - Huh?

157
07:42.045 --> 07:43.083
- Huh? - What?

158
07:43.083 --> 07:44.209
What?

159
07:44.209 --> 07:45.215
What do we do?

160
07:45.215 --> 07:47.509
What do you mean? Quit freezing up.

161
07:47.509 --> 07:49.719
Sergeant Choi...

162
07:49.719 --> 07:52.097
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu! - You're cadre now, you idiot...

163
07:52.097 --> 07:53.584
Follow me.

164
07:53.584 --> 07:55.459
Chungseong! Love you!

165
07:55.459 --> 07:57.584
Sorry...

166
07:57.584 --> 07:59.584
Those two look suspicious.

167
07:59.584 --> 08:01.751
They didn't even have a conversation.

168
08:03.525 --> 08:06.486
You little... You're a pretty good actor.

169
08:06.486 --> 08:09.918
"Sergeant Choi Il Gu!" I was in drama club in middle school.

170
08:09.918 --> 08:14.125
- So you've got some experience. - Wasn't I amazing?

171
08:14.125 --> 08:15.959
Smoking imported cigarettes now?

172
08:15.959 --> 08:18.709
This is Korea-U.S. joint training, isn't it?

173
08:18.709 --> 08:20.334
- Let's do some joint training. - Here, have one.

174
08:20.334 --> 08:21.937
Yeah.

175
08:26.459 --> 08:28.634
You guys are unbelievable... and you're cadre.

176
08:28.634 --> 08:31.167
He forced me to smoke it.

177
08:31.167 --> 08:33.972
You gave it to me. Joint training!

178
08:33.972 --> 08:37.183
Didn't you send me to buy these? You told me to buy them.

179
08:37.183 --> 08:40.103
- We were just going to smell them... - Wait...

180
08:40.103 --> 08:41.584
- I can't believe you'd do this. - Hey!

181
08:41.584 --> 08:43.231
- Hey. - Why are you sulking?

182
08:43.231 --> 08:45.120
Byeong Nam, this...

183
08:45.120 --> 08:47.500
We just smelled it. Come on.

184
08:47.500 --> 08:49.624
Byeong Nam, this is U.S. military issue.

185
08:49.624 --> 08:51.438
We were just checking...

186
08:52.241 --> 08:54.162
Hey! What...

187
08:56.125 --> 08:58.663
Why are you so sensitive?

188
08:58.663 --> 09:01.830
[Regimental Commander's Office]

189
09:10.626 --> 09:11.760
Written statement.

190
09:11.760 --> 09:16.626
95th Division, 45th Infantry Regiment, 7th Battalion, Byeon Hyeok Jin.

191
09:16.626 --> 09:19.768
Company Commander Cho Baek Ho merely followed procedure.

192
09:19.768 --> 09:23.646
As battalion commander, I attest that he had no intent

193
09:23.646 --> 09:26.441
to seek personal gain or evade responsibility.

194
09:26.441 --> 09:30.959
Rather, the fundamental responsibility for this incident lies with me.

195
09:30.959 --> 09:34.324
I created the unconventional unit cafe to break through the military's closed culture

196
09:34.324 --> 09:37.327
and failed to maintain security controls.

197
09:37.327 --> 09:38.379
[Byeon Hyeok Jin]

198
09:39.496 --> 09:41.373
Hey, Byeon Hyeok Jin.

199
09:41.373 --> 09:42.959
Are you kidding me?

200
09:42.959 --> 09:47.337
I heard the Second Company commander volunteered to take full responsibility.

201
09:47.337 --> 09:51.834
Then relieve him of command, report it to the division, and be done with it.

202
09:51.834 --> 09:54.761
What on earth is this?

203
09:54.761 --> 09:59.758
Sir, I wanted to fulfill my responsibilities as a commander.

204
09:59.758 --> 10:00.809
What?

205
10:00.809 --> 10:03.061
Since I took command, Company Commander Cho Baek Ho has followed

206
10:03.061 --> 10:05.751
my orders more faithfully than anyone.

207
10:05.751 --> 10:09.317
He trusted me enough to support the unconventional unit cafe.

208
10:09.317 --> 10:12.153
And it was Captain Cho Baek Ho who did everything he could

209
10:12.153 --> 10:14.167
on-site for troop morale,

210
10:14.167 --> 10:16.042
not to cover up the incident.

211
10:16.042 --> 10:17.250
That's exactly my point!

212
10:17.250 --> 10:21.871
From the outside, that on-site response looks like a cover-up!

213
10:21.871 --> 10:24.249
The media's tearing us apart.

214
10:24.249 --> 10:25.804
Someone has to take the fall

215
10:25.804 --> 10:28.626
so it at least looks like we're taking responsibility!

216
10:28.626 --> 10:33.049
I've always told my battalion that responsibility goes upward.

217
10:33.049 --> 10:36.719
If I dump this on Company Commander Cho Baek Ho,

218
10:36.719 --> 10:40.056
what officer could ever lead his unit with conviction?

219
10:40.056 --> 10:42.851
I believe we'd be undermining the command structure of our regiment,

220
10:42.851 --> 10:45.629
and ultimately the entire army.

221
10:47.167 --> 10:48.731
Hyeok Jin...

222
10:48.731 --> 10:51.609
Please, let's make this easy.

223
10:51.609 --> 10:53.319
You're doing well. Why are you doing this?

224
10:53.319 --> 10:56.355
Keep trying to protect everyone and you'll be the one who gets burned.

225
10:57.959 --> 10:59.659
Sir,

226
10:59.659 --> 11:03.204
I'll take care of myself.

227
11:03.204 --> 11:05.874
I'm sorry. I'll be going.

228
11:05.874 --> 11:07.751
Chungseong!

229
11:07.751 --> 11:09.909
Please make sure you get something to eat.

230
11:10.712 --> 11:12.381
Hyeok Jin!

231
11:12.381 --> 11:13.882
Byeon Hyeok Jin!

232
11:13.882 --> 11:15.627
Hey!

233
11:20.459 --> 11:23.083
Don't you remember individual combat training...

234
11:23.083 --> 11:24.803
at boot camp?

235
11:26.751 --> 11:31.900
- Individual Battle Drills! - Individual Battle Drills!

236
11:31.900 --> 11:34.736
[Week 4 of Boot Camp: Individual Battle Drills]

237
11:34.736 --> 11:38.239
We were about the same age,

238
11:38.239 --> 11:41.584
in the same boat, and after struggling together for a few weeks,

239
11:41.584 --> 11:44.204
- we got close fast. - What do I do...

240
11:44.204 --> 11:45.788
- Advance! - Stay low!

241
11:45.788 --> 11:47.575
Advance!

242
11:49.584 --> 11:50.709
Advance!

243
11:50.709 --> 11:52.751
Hey. Did you hear?

244
11:52.751 --> 11:56.883
One of our guys is the division commander's son.

245
11:56.883 --> 11:58.092
- Seriously? - Yeah.

246
11:58.092 --> 12:00.596
That's insane.

247
12:00.596 --> 12:02.542
Man, he's got it made in the army.

248
12:02.542 --> 12:04.834
I heard his last name's Park...

249
12:04.834 --> 12:06.336
Park?

250
12:07.334 --> 12:09.834
Hey, Park Min Seok, is it you?

251
12:09.834 --> 12:11.239
What?

252
12:13.733 --> 12:15.109
Huh?

253
12:15.109 --> 12:16.612
Look at him.

254
12:16.612 --> 12:20.000
If he were the division commander's son, would he be here like this?

255
12:20.000 --> 12:22.116
Exactly.

256
12:22.116 --> 12:25.014
Hey! The instructor's coming.

257
12:27.247 --> 12:29.207
All right, next group! Get ready! Move it!

258
12:29.207 --> 12:30.760
- Yes! - Yes!

259
12:32.000 --> 12:34.337
Cho Je Uk, you got this! Don't get hurt!

260
12:34.337 --> 12:37.167
You got this! Stay safe!

261
12:37.167 --> 12:39.667
- Prone position! - Prone position!

262
12:39.667 --> 12:42.595
- My knees are going to get scraped raw. - Next group, move out!

263
12:42.595 --> 12:43.638
Understood!

264
12:43.638 --> 12:46.083
- All right, let's go! - Move it, move it!

265
12:46.083 --> 12:48.000
You got this!

266
12:48.000 --> 12:49.102
Min Seok.

267
12:49.102 --> 12:51.209
When it's our turn, just follow me!

268
12:51.209 --> 12:53.834
Okay. Thanks.

269
12:53.834 --> 12:55.553
Get down and fire!

270
12:57.250 --> 12:58.959
Next group, move out.

271
12:58.959 --> 13:01.137
- Understood! - Move out!

272
13:04.751 --> 13:06.584
- Advance! - Advance!

273
13:06.584 --> 13:08.785
Get through the wire!

274
13:14.167 --> 13:17.207
You can do this, Park Min Seok!

275
13:26.932 --> 13:28.308
Incoming!

276
13:28.308 --> 13:30.371
- Incoming! - Incoming!

277
13:31.853 --> 13:33.396
Min Seok!

278
13:33.396 --> 13:36.116
You need to stand up! Stay up!

279
13:37.984 --> 13:40.882
- Advance! - Advance!

280
13:44.825 --> 13:47.417
I had no idea what was about to happen that day...

281
13:47.417 --> 13:50.413
or that you'd lie to me like that.

282
13:50.413 --> 13:53.041
- You, Park Min Seok... - Min Seok!

283
13:53.041 --> 13:55.793
- Park Min Seok! - Park Min Seok!

284
13:55.793 --> 13:57.112
Corporal Park Min Seok!

285
13:57.112 --> 13:59.584
What are you doing with the water running?

286
13:59.584 --> 14:01.090
I was brushing my teeth.

287
14:01.090 --> 14:04.799
- Get ready for duty. - Yes. I'll be right out.

288
14:08.723 --> 14:11.978
All personnel, assemble for company work detail.

289
14:13.745 --> 14:14.937
Careful!

290
14:14.937 --> 14:16.314
- Put it down! - Yes!

291
14:16.314 --> 14:18.066
Careful.

292
14:18.066 --> 14:19.363
There.

293
14:21.028 --> 14:23.363
Why is every work detail always such a damn mess?

294
14:23.363 --> 14:25.292
That's the army for you.

295
14:25.292 --> 14:26.626
I need to get out of here...

296
14:26.626 --> 14:27.867
Hey.

297
14:27.867 --> 14:29.834
What's with these two now?

298
14:29.834 --> 14:31.162
They feel betrayed.

299
14:31.162 --> 14:32.414
Betrayed?

300
14:32.414 --> 14:34.584
You really can't trust anyone in this world.

301
14:34.584 --> 14:37.293
The assistant platoon leader and Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu

302
14:37.293 --> 14:39.128
were acting suspicious, so I followed them.

303
14:39.128 --> 14:42.000
Turns out they were sneaking cigarettes...

304
14:42.000 --> 14:44.760
Seriously? Man... that's betrayal.

305
14:44.760 --> 14:46.594
They're always busting our asses.

306
14:46.594 --> 14:48.125
I need to get home.

307
14:48.125 --> 14:51.250
Getting out is the only way to survive this crap.

308
14:51.250 --> 14:52.643
Exactly.

309
14:52.643 --> 14:54.918
Hey, how many days till we're out?

310
14:54.918 --> 14:56.187
Come on, let's finish this and go.

311
14:56.187 --> 14:57.334
- Yes! - Yes!

312
14:57.334 --> 14:59.798
Come on, man. At least give me a reaction.

313
14:59.798 --> 15:00.858
A reaction...

314
15:00.858 --> 15:03.626
I still respect you two.

315
15:03.626 --> 15:05.363
You're almost out, but you still show up for work details.

316
15:05.363 --> 15:08.353
What's the point of hiding out? It just makes time go slower.

317
15:09.834 --> 15:11.619
Chungseong! Love you!

318
15:11.619 --> 15:13.287
Nice work.

319
15:13.287 --> 15:14.959
Take a ten-minute break right here.

320
15:14.959 --> 15:16.500
- Ten-minute break! - Ten-minute break!

321
15:16.500 --> 15:19.085
Smokers, go ahead and smoke. Everyone else, take a break.

322
15:19.085 --> 15:20.711
Man, I'm jealous.

323
15:20.711 --> 15:23.459
A cigarette after a work detail is the best.

324
15:23.459 --> 15:26.287
Takes all the fatigue away.

325
15:27.719 --> 15:29.928
I'm craving one more by the second.

326
15:30.667 --> 15:32.224
That looks freaking good.

327
15:32.224 --> 15:34.226
It's freaking beautiful.

328
15:34.226 --> 15:36.102
What if they start a wildfire?

329
15:36.102 --> 15:38.052
That's reward money right there!

330
15:39.417 --> 15:40.481
Break's over!

331
15:40.481 --> 15:42.500
- Break's over! - Grab the brooms. And those shovels.

332
15:42.500 --> 15:44.751
Chungseong! Love you! Take care, sir!

333
15:44.751 --> 15:46.709
- Take care, sir! - Take care, sir!

334
15:46.709 --> 15:48.913
Look at those damn slackers.

335
15:50.867 --> 15:52.869
It fell out!

336
15:52.869 --> 15:54.500
- What are you doing? - Where are you going?

337
15:54.500 --> 15:56.089
Where are you going?

338
16:00.125 --> 16:02.240
Anything in it?

339
16:05.667 --> 16:08.292
Man... a cigarette!

340
16:08.292 --> 16:09.626
Oh! A cigarette!

341
16:09.626 --> 16:10.845
It's a real cigarette.

342
16:10.845 --> 16:13.389
Come on... it's The Two 0.1.

343
16:13.389 --> 16:15.391
That's basically like not smoking at all.

344
16:15.391 --> 16:16.851
You idiot.

345
16:16.851 --> 16:19.854
It's only 0.1 mg. But if you wrap your lips around the filter and take a deep drag,

346
16:19.854 --> 16:21.626
it hits like five!

347
16:21.626 --> 16:22.815
So who's smoking it?

348
16:22.815 --> 16:24.250
Obviously me. I found it...

349
16:24.250 --> 16:26.652
What are you talking about? You want to lose that hand?

350
16:26.652 --> 16:28.863
We go by seniority.

351
16:29.542 --> 16:30.823
We found it together.

352
16:30.823 --> 16:31.959
What?

353
16:31.959 --> 16:35.077
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, didn't I do more shoveling earlier?

354
16:35.077 --> 16:36.913
This should go by who worked the hardest.

355
16:36.913 --> 16:38.915
Did you forget our squad's overnight pass is on the line?

356
16:38.915 --> 16:40.250
If even one of us smokes it,

357
16:40.250 --> 16:43.252
it'll show up on the nicotine test, and we lose the pass.

358
16:43.252 --> 16:45.918
Right... the pass.

359
16:45.918 --> 16:48.049
Yeah... let's hold out a little longer.

360
16:48.049 --> 16:51.052
Or we could each take one drag. Huh?

361
16:51.052 --> 16:53.095
One drag won't even show up.

362
16:53.095 --> 16:54.889
It's practically secondhand smoke.

363
16:54.889 --> 16:57.433
Exactly. Just one tiny drag each.

364
16:57.433 --> 16:58.542
Hold on.

365
16:58.542 --> 17:01.125
Let's leave it to the squad leader.

366
17:01.125 --> 17:04.277
Kim Dong Woo, you decide.

367
17:05.876 --> 17:07.493
Let's...

368
17:13.407 --> 17:15.500
make it to that overnight pass.

369
17:15.500 --> 17:17.412
Then you can get out,

370
17:17.412 --> 17:19.038
breathe civilian air instead of dirt,

371
17:19.038 --> 17:22.292
and enjoy...

372
17:22.292 --> 17:24.126
a proper cigarette.

373
17:24.126 --> 17:25.503
You've held out this long.

374
17:25.503 --> 17:27.125
- Just a little longer! - Yes!

375
17:27.125 --> 17:28.673
- Yes! - That's right.

376
17:28.673 --> 17:31.050
Once we're out, let's buy a pack of Marlboro Lights.

377
17:31.050 --> 17:34.054
Then what do we do with this?

378
17:34.054 --> 17:35.180
Where are you going?

379
17:35.180 --> 17:36.430
- Stop him! - Stop him!

380
17:36.430 --> 17:38.057
No! Don't!

381
17:38.057 --> 17:40.061
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

382
17:49.653 --> 17:51.554
What are you doing?

383
17:57.792 --> 17:58.953
What is he doing?

384
17:58.953 --> 18:00.776
I don't know.

385
18:17.417 --> 18:19.709
Under the crooked pine.

386
18:19.709 --> 18:23.174
Someday, when we're finally free of this no-smoking curse,

387
18:23.811 --> 18:26.375
we'll come back and smoke it.

388
18:26.375 --> 18:28.899
Come on, let's go finish the job.

389
18:28.899 --> 18:30.375
- Yes. - Yes.

390
18:30.375 --> 18:31.792
Bring him back.

391
18:31.792 --> 18:34.167
- We should get going. - We should get going.

392
18:34.167 --> 18:35.740
It's only a few more days.

393
18:35.740 --> 18:37.709
We just have to hold out until the test.

394
18:37.709 --> 18:39.647
We should get going...

395
18:41.000 --> 18:42.622
It's hot. Let's get this done.

396
18:42.622 --> 18:43.873
- Yes. - Yes.

397
18:43.873 --> 18:46.459
If we don't do this right, we'll just have to do it again later.

398
18:46.459 --> 18:47.859
Got it.

399
18:50.083 --> 18:51.714
Dig harder! Come on!

400
18:51.714 --> 18:53.456
Yes!

401
18:55.584 --> 18:58.471
Da Hye, switch with Bit Na Ri.

402
18:58.471 --> 19:00.015
No, I'm fine!

403
19:00.015 --> 19:02.516
You look like you're about to drop. Switch out.

404
19:02.516 --> 19:03.999
I'll take over.

405
19:04.894 --> 19:06.125
Thank you.

406
19:06.125 --> 19:08.542
Why are you sweating so much?

407
19:08.542 --> 19:10.191
- Thank you. - Yeah.

408
19:10.191 --> 19:11.984
- Hey, Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok!

409
19:11.984 --> 19:14.111
Where'd Hyeon Uk go?

410
19:14.111 --> 19:15.918
Hyeon Uk went to get the bag...

411
19:15.918 --> 19:18.366
Oh, there he is with it!

412
19:18.366 --> 19:19.660
Hurry up, will you?

413
19:19.660 --> 19:21.619
- Sorry! - This slacker...

414
19:21.619 --> 19:23.329
- Get over here! - Here, give that to me.

415
19:23.329 --> 19:25.341
Hurry up.

416
19:31.209 --> 19:33.000
Are you okay?

417
19:33.000 --> 19:34.965
Are you okay?

418
19:34.965 --> 19:37.468
Take care of that precious body of yours.

419
19:37.468 --> 19:39.751
Whose life are you trying to ruin this time?

420
19:39.751 --> 19:41.250
What?

421
19:41.250 --> 19:43.284
- Advance! - Advance!

422
19:50.566 --> 19:51.732
Min Seok!

423
19:51.732 --> 19:53.150
Are you okay?

424
19:53.150 --> 19:55.417
Yeah, I'm okay. Go on without me!

425
19:55.417 --> 19:57.437
Trainee 12!

426
19:59.490 --> 20:01.158
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok!

427
20:01.158 --> 20:03.985
- Are you okay? - Yes, I'm fine!

428
20:05.375 --> 20:06.789
Fall out!

429
20:06.789 --> 20:08.042
Grab my hand.

430
20:08.042 --> 20:10.000
- Come on. - Falling out!

431
20:10.000 --> 20:11.367
Does it hurt?

432
20:12.083 --> 20:13.129
How about now?

433
20:13.129 --> 20:16.633
I think I just twisted it a little. I should be okay.

434
20:16.633 --> 20:18.801
- Try moving it. - Okay.

435
20:18.801 --> 20:20.302
Trainee 12.

436
20:20.302 --> 20:22.138
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok!

437
20:22.138 --> 20:23.597
Your buddies are still out there. You want to quit?

438
20:23.597 --> 20:25.558
- No! - Can you keep going?

439
20:25.558 --> 20:27.268
Yes! I can keep going!

440
20:27.268 --> 20:28.519
Spray his ankle.

441
20:28.519 --> 20:30.389
Yes.

442
20:33.190 --> 20:35.234
What happened?

443
20:35.234 --> 20:36.417
Chungseong.

444
20:36.417 --> 20:38.584
I think he twisted his ankle while running.

445
20:38.584 --> 20:39.947
Again?

446
20:39.947 --> 20:43.200
The old "I don't want to march" routine?

447
20:43.200 --> 20:44.635
Chungseong.

448
20:46.203 --> 20:47.329
Trainee 12!

449
20:47.329 --> 20:50.792
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok!

450
20:50.792 --> 20:52.167
Park Min Seok?

451
20:52.167 --> 20:54.500
You have the division commander's son in your company, right?

452
20:54.500 --> 20:56.548
Seriously? My company?

453
20:56.548 --> 20:58.340
- You didn't know? - Nothing unusual in the reports.

454
20:58.340 --> 21:00.667
Of course they kept it secret.

455
21:00.667 --> 21:02.386
You tell me this now?

456
21:02.386 --> 21:06.638
I only happened to overhear the adjutant telling the battalion commander yesterday.

457
21:06.638 --> 21:09.144
Damn it...

458
21:09.144 --> 21:10.500
What's his name?

459
21:10.500 --> 21:11.751
Park something...

460
21:11.751 --> 21:13.667
Park Min Sik? Or was it Seok Min?

461
21:13.667 --> 21:16.068
You don't even know his name?

462
21:16.068 --> 21:19.204
Park Min Seok! Right, it was Park Min Seok.

463
21:20.656 --> 21:23.492
So you're Trainee 12, Park Min Seok.

464
21:23.492 --> 21:25.489
Yes, that's right.

465
21:27.453 --> 21:31.582
Even with such a serious injury, you were determined to get back to training.

466
21:31.582 --> 21:35.093
That's the attitude of a true soldier.

467
21:36.088 --> 21:39.459
Just to be safe, get him transported right away.

468
21:39.459 --> 21:41.584
Right now?

469
21:41.584 --> 21:42.760
"Right now?"

470
21:42.760 --> 21:44.261
Yes, right now! Immediately!

471
21:44.261 --> 21:48.307
It may look minor, but who knows what could happen later?

472
21:48.307 --> 21:49.375
I suppose so.

473
21:49.375 --> 21:51.393
But I really think I'll be fine

474
21:51.393 --> 21:53.938
- if I rest a little. - No.

475
21:53.938 --> 21:59.617
Looking after my trainees' health is my duty as the company commander.

476
22:00.946 --> 22:03.866
Listen to me, Trainee Park Min Seok!

477
22:03.866 --> 22:05.771
Yes!

478
22:07.119 --> 22:09.667
What are you waiting for? Hurry up and escort him...

479
22:09.667 --> 22:10.871
I mean, take him!

480
22:10.871 --> 22:12.915
Yes! I'll get ready to leave right away.

481
22:12.915 --> 22:14.425
Chungseong!

482
22:17.167 --> 22:18.778
Chungseong!

483
22:19.417 --> 22:20.958
Thank you!

484
22:23.751 --> 22:25.429
Wait!

485
22:25.429 --> 22:28.209
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok!

486
22:28.209 --> 22:32.019
Eat this on the way. Keep your blood sugar up.

487
22:32.019 --> 22:33.602
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok!

488
22:33.602 --> 22:34.770
Thank you!

489
22:34.770 --> 22:36.690
- Let's go. - Yes.

490
22:36.690 --> 22:37.706
Thank you.

491
22:37.706 --> 22:39.316
You know I'm the company commander here, right?

492
22:39.316 --> 22:43.237
Yes, I know. Thank you, sir.

493
22:43.237 --> 22:45.610
Stay in formation.

494
22:50.369 --> 22:52.204
Trainee 11.

495
22:52.204 --> 22:53.747
Trainee 11, Kim Hyeon Uk!

496
22:53.747 --> 22:55.792
What happened?

497
22:55.792 --> 22:59.086
I landed wrong after jumping an obstacle,

498
22:59.086 --> 23:00.751
and my knee feels off.

499
23:00.751 --> 23:01.755
Be careful.

500
23:01.755 --> 23:03.069
Okay.

501
23:04.209 --> 23:06.125
Hyeon Uk!

502
23:06.125 --> 23:08.804
- Are you hurt? - Yeah...

503
23:08.804 --> 23:11.375
I'm okay.

504
23:11.375 --> 23:12.433
Min Seok, are you okay?

505
23:12.433 --> 23:13.851
Yeah, I'm fine.

506
23:13.851 --> 23:15.019
I'll wait for you!

507
23:15.019 --> 23:16.712
- Okay. - Yeah.

508
23:20.918 --> 23:23.068
Now what? Another injury?

509
23:23.068 --> 23:25.125
Yes.

510
23:25.125 --> 23:27.031
This is driving me crazy.

511
23:27.031 --> 23:28.240
What happened?

512
23:28.240 --> 23:31.452
I landed wrong after jumping an obstacle,

513
23:31.452 --> 23:33.829
and my knee hurts a little.

514
23:33.829 --> 23:35.122
Can you move?

515
23:35.122 --> 23:37.184
I can, but...

516
23:37.834 --> 23:39.294
my knee is...

517
23:39.294 --> 23:40.294
Does that hurt?

518
23:40.294 --> 23:42.046
It feels weird.

519
23:42.046 --> 23:44.030
It hurts!

520
23:45.215 --> 23:48.059
Sir, could you come over here for a second?

521
23:53.834 --> 23:56.393
I think he may have injured a ligament.

522
23:56.393 --> 23:57.394
Is it serious?

523
23:57.394 --> 23:59.565
I can't tell yet.

524
23:59.565 --> 24:02.157
He should get examined.

525
24:02.900 --> 24:04.193
The battalion commander said

526
24:04.193 --> 24:06.528
we'll be penalized for too many medical evacuations.

527
24:06.528 --> 24:09.064
He told us to do a better job preventing injuries.

528
24:16.792 --> 24:18.709
Leave now with him.

529
24:18.709 --> 24:21.962
Pull that one from training and send him back to the unit.

530
24:21.962 --> 24:24.546
You mean leave now with this patient?

531
24:24.546 --> 24:26.341
Didn't you hear me?

532
24:26.341 --> 24:29.166
Yes. Chungseong.

533
24:37.375 --> 24:39.019
Isn't he coming with us?

534
24:39.019 --> 24:41.500
Use some pain-relief spray and rest. You'll be fine.

535
24:41.500 --> 24:43.565
I'll excuse you from training.

536
24:43.565 --> 24:45.442
Take care of him.

537
24:45.442 --> 24:47.167
Understood!

538
24:47.167 --> 24:48.704
Hyeon Uk!

539
25:00.125 --> 25:03.001
Then what about me?

540
25:03.001 --> 25:05.254
Can you walk?

541
25:05.254 --> 25:06.739
Take my arm.

542
25:20.019 --> 25:23.134
You okay? Does it really hurt?

543
25:23.941 --> 25:25.065
A little...

544
25:25.065 --> 25:28.409
I thought you were faking it to get out of the march.

545
25:29.000 --> 25:32.616
I'm not Park Min Seok. Why would I fake it?

546
25:32.616 --> 25:35.007
It does feel pretty bad, though.

547
25:35.626 --> 25:37.667
Maybe it'll be better after I sleep.

548
25:37.667 --> 25:40.167
He's even trying to fool us.

549
25:40.167 --> 25:42.465
I'm serious...

550
25:45.083 --> 25:46.837
Want me to tell the instructor?

551
25:46.837 --> 25:48.756
I did.

552
25:48.756 --> 25:51.209
He said to wait and see until tomorrow.

553
25:51.209 --> 25:52.801
Thanks, Tae Woong...

554
25:52.801 --> 25:54.336
Yeah.

555
25:55.345 --> 25:57.473
Min Seok's really gone.

556
25:57.473 --> 26:01.143
I didn't think he'd actually get sent out like that.

557
26:01.143 --> 26:04.021
Must be nice for Min Seok.

558
26:04.021 --> 26:07.824
He might really be hurt...

559
26:09.000 --> 26:10.855
I guess...

560
26:52.220 --> 26:53.237
Attention.

561
26:53.237 --> 26:54.613
- Attention! - Attention!

562
26:54.613 --> 26:57.503
Trainee Kim Hyeon Uk was rushed to the emergency room early today.

563
26:57.503 --> 26:58.951
Just so you're aware.

564
26:58.951 --> 27:00.005
Understood?

565
27:00.005 --> 27:01.669
- Yes! - Yes!

566
27:02.876 --> 27:04.873
Trainee Number 9, Kwon Tae Woong!

567
27:04.873 --> 27:06.166
May I ask a question?

568
27:06.166 --> 27:07.751
What is it? Make it quick.

569
27:07.751 --> 27:10.428
Is he badly hurt?

570
27:12.339 --> 27:15.092
I don't know. Don't worry about it. Just focus on training.

571
27:15.092 --> 27:17.644
- Got it? - Understood.

572
27:20.918 --> 27:23.125
- Guess Hyeon Uk really was hurt. - Yeah...

573
27:23.125 --> 27:25.185
What if something's seriously wrong with Hyeon Uk?

574
27:25.185 --> 27:27.751
He was in a lot of pain yesterday. Think he broke a bone?

575
27:27.751 --> 27:30.899
That did look pretty serious yesterday.

576
27:30.899 --> 27:33.355
Yeah. This is bad.

577
27:34.570 --> 27:36.275
[Armed Forces Central Hospital]

578
27:39.535 --> 27:43.876
It looks like you may have torn your anterior cruciate ligament.

579
27:43.876 --> 27:48.125
You must've felt something when it happened.

580
27:48.125 --> 27:51.420
You should've told the instructor right away.

581
27:51.420 --> 27:53.584
Why'd you just keep quiet?

582
27:53.584 --> 27:55.132
I did tell him.

583
27:55.132 --> 27:56.842
Did you make it clear?

584
27:56.842 --> 27:59.500
It's your body. You have to look after yourself.

585
27:59.500 --> 28:01.346
I could still move around a little, so...

586
28:01.346 --> 28:03.350
You still should've come in right away.

587
28:03.350 --> 28:05.855
Why'd you let it get this bad?

588
28:09.855 --> 28:11.356
So what's going to happen to me?

589
28:11.356 --> 28:13.817
We'll know once the medical review comes back.

590
28:13.817 --> 28:15.866
It'll take a while.

591
28:16.459 --> 28:18.830
Wait outside for now, okay?

592
28:20.449 --> 28:22.116
Understood...

593
28:32.085 --> 28:35.424
Didn't a trainee come in from the training camp yesterday?

594
28:35.424 --> 28:38.250
That trainee was discharged this morning.

595
28:38.250 --> 28:39.676
They're from the same place.

596
28:39.676 --> 28:42.639
Why didn't they send that kid in the same ambulance?

597
28:42.639 --> 28:44.890
He clearly looked worse.

598
28:44.890 --> 28:47.834
I'm not sure, but...

599
28:47.834 --> 28:51.832
Apparently, he was the Division Commander's son.

600
28:51.832 --> 28:52.858
What?

601
28:52.858 --> 28:56.693
They said Trainee Park Min Seok is the Division Commander's son.

602
28:56.693 --> 28:58.195
Come on.

603
28:58.195 --> 29:00.864
You should've told me something like that right away!

604
29:00.864 --> 29:03.659
I'm sorry. I only found out when they called later

605
29:03.659 --> 29:06.083
and told us to take good care of him.

606
29:06.083 --> 29:09.464
I would've treated him a little nicer...

607
29:10.209 --> 29:13.718
So that's why he came in the ambulance alone.

608
29:14.709 --> 29:17.138
That poor kid's the one who got screwed...

609
29:21.385 --> 29:23.042
Excuse me...

610
29:23.042 --> 29:24.083
Yes?

611
29:24.083 --> 29:26.014
Well...

612
29:26.014 --> 29:29.834
Is Trainee Park Min Seok... the Division Commander's son?

613
29:29.834 --> 29:32.598
Yes. That's what I heard.

614
29:34.064 --> 29:36.901
One of our guys is the division commander's son.

615
29:36.901 --> 29:38.110
I heard his last name is Park...

616
29:38.110 --> 29:39.459
Hey, Park Min Seok, is it you?

617
29:39.459 --> 29:40.766
What?

618
29:42.115 --> 29:44.066
I'll excuse you from training.

619
29:47.246 --> 29:49.204
Must be nice for Min Seok.

620
29:49.204 --> 29:52.646
He might really be hurt...

621
29:54.125 --> 29:57.595
So that's why he came in the ambulance alone.

622
29:59.083 --> 30:02.475
That poor kid's the one who got screwed...

623
30:04.751 --> 30:06.820
Damn it.

624
30:08.250 --> 30:09.268
Seriously?

625
30:09.268 --> 30:11.042
Did you see Min Seok fall earlier?

626
30:11.042 --> 30:13.500
What are you talking about? I didn't fall.

627
30:13.500 --> 30:16.000
That wasn't me falling...

628
30:16.000 --> 30:19.109
Trainee Kim Hyeon Uk has a torn anterior cruciate ligament

629
30:19.109 --> 30:22.612
and is medically unfit to continue training.

630
30:22.612 --> 30:25.784
The medical review has determined that he will be sent home.

631
30:25.784 --> 30:28.201
After he leaves the training camp,

632
30:28.201 --> 30:31.493
his return to service will depend on his recovery from surgery.

633
30:32.083 --> 30:33.742
The army is...

634
30:35.709 --> 30:37.458
terrible...

635
30:38.754 --> 30:40.629
and so is Park Min Seok.

636
30:53.310 --> 30:55.687
Corporal Park Min Seok,

637
30:55.687 --> 30:58.083
has something been bothering you lately?

638
30:58.083 --> 30:59.590
Bothering me?

639
31:00.861 --> 31:03.945
Everyone's got something to worry about.

640
31:03.945 --> 31:05.909
That's true.

641
31:07.626 --> 31:10.911
Still, you've got it good.

642
31:10.911 --> 31:12.120
How so?

643
31:12.120 --> 31:15.499
Just looking in the mirror gives me something to worry about.

644
31:15.499 --> 31:17.584
You look like you don't have a care in the world.

645
31:17.584 --> 31:19.878
Come on, what are you talking about?

646
31:19.878 --> 31:22.297
I've got plenty to worry about too.

647
31:22.297 --> 31:25.384
- You do? - Of course I do.

648
31:25.384 --> 31:28.303
I worry about whether I can get back to what I was doing once I get out,

649
31:28.303 --> 31:31.807
and about my mom's health too.

650
31:31.807 --> 31:34.226
Oh, right! How's your mother doing?

651
31:34.226 --> 31:36.436
She's doing much better.

652
31:36.436 --> 31:37.584
That's good to hear.

653
31:37.584 --> 31:39.898
Thank you.

654
31:39.898 --> 31:43.318
That's one thing I like about the army.

655
31:43.318 --> 31:46.680
People worry about you and look out for you.

656
31:47.459 --> 31:49.209
There's one more thing I'm worried about.

657
31:49.209 --> 31:52.285
- What? - What kind of ramen to eat after our shift!

658
31:52.285 --> 31:54.542
Oh, yeah.

659
31:54.542 --> 31:58.961
And what Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam will say in his sleep tonight,

660
31:58.961 --> 32:02.671
whether Corporal Kim Dong Woo will sleep well,

661
32:02.671 --> 32:08.935
and whether Corporal Ji Jeong Min will make it to night watch on time tonight.

662
32:12.139 --> 32:14.808
You really do have a lot on your mind.

663
32:14.808 --> 32:16.433
Not really.

664
32:17.060 --> 32:19.563
I've got some Sichuan Chapagetti too.

665
32:19.563 --> 32:22.717
- Let me know if you want some later. - Thank you!

666
32:26.959 --> 32:30.552
I know all about it.

667
32:31.626 --> 32:33.660
Seriously?

668
32:33.660 --> 32:35.120
How?

669
32:35.120 --> 32:38.005
You must have a lot to worry about...

670
32:39.667 --> 32:41.675
every time you look in the mirror.

671
32:42.459 --> 32:44.006
What?

672
32:44.006 --> 32:46.751
Oh, come on!

673
32:46.751 --> 32:47.924
Sorry.

674
32:47.924 --> 32:51.792
You looked really worried, so I wanted to make you laugh.

675
32:51.792 --> 32:53.083
You scared me.

676
32:53.083 --> 32:54.181
Well, it worked!

677
32:54.181 --> 32:56.524
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

678
32:57.250 --> 32:58.977
You actually got me to laugh.

679
32:58.977 --> 33:01.028
Thanks, Se Gye.

680
33:04.149 --> 33:06.653
Anytime you need me, just say the word.

681
33:06.653 --> 33:08.530
I may not be able to fix it,

682
33:08.530 --> 33:10.258
but I can at least...

683
33:10.864 --> 33:13.292
talk it through with you.

684
33:14.542 --> 33:15.986
Yeah.

685
33:34.500 --> 33:37.565
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, back from duty.

686
33:41.146 --> 33:43.091
You scared me...

687
33:44.147 --> 33:46.709
Why are you still up?

688
33:46.709 --> 33:49.876
I can't sleep. Must be withdrawal.

689
33:49.876 --> 33:52.334
Should I get you some water?

690
33:52.334 --> 33:55.333
I think I've already had like ten liters.

691
34:01.167 --> 34:02.834
I'm going to the bathroom...

692
34:02.834 --> 34:05.120
Understood.

693
34:08.841 --> 34:11.307
Withdrawal?

694
34:12.801 --> 34:15.615
[Day 3 of Quitting Smoking]

695
34:21.125 --> 34:22.996
I want to sleep...

696
34:36.157 --> 34:37.959
You scared me!

697
34:39.746 --> 34:41.162
What?

698
34:41.162 --> 34:42.709
What's wrong with him?

699
34:42.709 --> 34:45.333
He was acting strange when I got back from duty last night...

700
34:45.333 --> 34:49.629
He's always been weird, but he's way weirder today.

701
34:49.629 --> 34:52.375
Looks like serious withdrawal.

702
34:52.375 --> 34:55.492
Are you okay?

703
34:57.973 --> 35:00.348
Welcome, my friends!

704
35:00.348 --> 35:02.601
Jeon Se Gye! Long time no see!

705
35:02.601 --> 35:04.978
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

706
35:04.978 --> 35:07.522
You've got a Physical Training uniform on. You're a real soldier now.

707
35:07.522 --> 35:09.441
- Hey, Dong Woo. - Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

708
35:09.441 --> 35:12.027
See? What'd I tell you?

709
35:12.027 --> 35:14.321
I told you one of your juniors was Jeon Se Gye

710
35:14.321 --> 35:16.615
and he'd come find me someday.

711
35:16.615 --> 35:17.949
That's my squad leader.

712
35:17.949 --> 35:20.500
He's great at getting things done, so I keep him around.

713
35:20.500 --> 35:22.167
Has he completely lost it?

714
35:22.167 --> 35:23.500
I think he's totally gone.

715
35:23.500 --> 35:25.040
My cigarettes... in the trash...

716
35:25.040 --> 35:26.207
Bring me my cigarettes!

717
35:26.207 --> 35:28.292
Where are they? Get them!

718
35:28.292 --> 35:30.660
Please look over there.

719
35:32.626 --> 35:33.840
Cigarettes...

720
35:33.840 --> 35:35.926
Cigarettes!

721
35:38.136 --> 35:40.375
It's not a cigarette.

722
35:40.375 --> 35:43.125
Does seeing something like a cigarette get your lungs racing?

723
35:43.125 --> 35:44.434
Excuse me?

724
35:44.434 --> 35:45.834
It's okay.

725
35:45.834 --> 35:48.584
When your nicotine wears off,

726
35:48.584 --> 35:51.991
you get cold and confused like this.

727
35:52.817 --> 35:56.446
When I'm a total wreck later, you guys better take care of me.

728
35:56.446 --> 35:57.447
Got it?

729
35:57.447 --> 35:59.699
- Understood. - Understood.

730
35:59.699 --> 36:01.910
- Se Gye... - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

731
36:01.910 --> 36:03.953
Later,

732
36:03.953 --> 36:06.748
when I'm old and can't pull this seniority crap anymore,

733
36:06.748 --> 36:08.667
if I come find you...

734
36:08.667 --> 36:10.751
- will you get me a deuce-and-a-half? - What?

735
36:10.751 --> 36:13.125
- A deuce... - A deuce-and-a-half? You mean the truck?

736
36:13.125 --> 36:17.175
♪ Riding a sleigh through the white snow... ♪

737
36:17.175 --> 36:19.447
♪ What a refreshing... ♪

738
36:20.261 --> 36:22.542
♪ feeling... ♪

739
36:22.542 --> 36:23.709
Refreshing?

740
36:23.709 --> 36:25.042
Dong Woo.

741
36:25.042 --> 36:27.000
- Chan Seok. - What?

742
36:27.000 --> 36:28.667
Refreshing...

743
36:28.667 --> 36:30.814
Refreshing!

744
36:30.814 --> 36:32.250
- Where are you going? - Grab him!

745
36:32.250 --> 36:34.442
- He's going for a smoke! - Hey! Grab him!

746
36:34.442 --> 36:36.083
No!

747
36:36.083 --> 36:37.542
- Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam! - Stop!

748
36:37.542 --> 36:39.417
- Grab him! - Grab him!

749
36:39.417 --> 36:41.667
- Chungseong! Love you! - Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

750
36:41.667 --> 36:43.542
You have to hold out!

751
36:43.542 --> 36:44.994
- Why are you doing this? - Come on!

752
36:44.994 --> 36:47.129
Why are you doing this?

753
36:54.584 --> 36:56.047
- Your shoes! - Where are you going?

754
36:56.047 --> 36:58.083
Cigarettes!

755
36:58.083 --> 36:59.559
Cigarettes.

756
37:04.042 --> 37:06.232
Hey, hide!

757
37:10.250 --> 37:11.521
Traitors...

758
37:11.521 --> 37:12.876
What happened to his face?

759
37:12.876 --> 37:15.241
Those guys are nuts.

760
37:19.167 --> 37:20.572
That's right!

761
37:20.572 --> 37:22.042
Where do you keep going?

762
37:22.042 --> 37:24.709
This is seriously dangerous! Wait!

763
37:24.709 --> 37:25.876
Is he a zombie or what?

764
37:25.876 --> 37:28.959
It's withdrawal! He's in withdrawal!

765
37:28.959 --> 37:31.924
Shouldn't we send Byeong Nam to the infirmary?

766
37:39.542 --> 37:41.376
He's way too fast.

767
37:54.751 --> 37:56.636
Are you out of your mind?

768
38:17.042 --> 38:18.795
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!

769
38:27.334 --> 38:28.876
Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

770
38:28.876 --> 38:30.733
Me too...

771
38:35.626 --> 38:37.815
That was bliss...

772
38:37.815 --> 38:39.459
What are we going to do?

773
38:39.459 --> 38:41.869
We have a urine test today...

774
38:42.779 --> 38:47.077
There goes our group overnight pass...

775
38:47.077 --> 38:49.246
Forget the overnight pass.

776
38:49.246 --> 38:52.789
Can't we just have fun like we're on an overnight pass?

777
38:52.789 --> 38:55.333
That's not the same...

778
38:55.333 --> 38:57.949
It's time for roll call.

779
39:06.052 --> 39:08.432
[Yooncheon Public Health Center]

780
39:09.500 --> 39:12.350
One little moment of pleasure...

781
39:12.350 --> 39:13.959
and our group overnight pass is gone.

782
39:13.959 --> 39:15.979
It's my fault. I should've stopped you guys.

783
39:15.979 --> 39:17.063
No.

784
39:17.063 --> 39:19.232
It's because I was useless.

785
39:19.232 --> 39:21.867
Better days will come.

786
39:24.615 --> 39:26.370
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam?

787
39:26.370 --> 39:28.744
- What? - Do you have a sec?

788
39:28.744 --> 39:31.622
What kind of junior makes his senior come to him?

789
39:31.622 --> 39:34.691
Heaven hasn't abandoned us.

790
39:35.792 --> 39:37.500
Look over there.

791
39:37.500 --> 39:39.417
Fill this with a urine sample and bring it back.

792
39:39.417 --> 39:42.792
The soldiers are handling their own urine test kits.

793
39:42.792 --> 39:46.792
So as long as the urine is clean, we're good, right?

794
39:46.792 --> 39:47.834
Right.

795
39:47.834 --> 39:51.188
And over there...

796
39:55.500 --> 39:58.918
I have a buddy with pristine,

797
39:58.918 --> 40:01.224
crystal-clear Grade-A urine.

798
40:02.709 --> 40:04.569
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

799
40:04.569 --> 40:06.991
You mean... my urine?

800
40:07.824 --> 40:10.834
Please don't stare so much. It's embarrassing!

801
40:10.834 --> 40:14.020
Bit Na Ri... help us just this once.

802
40:15.042 --> 40:19.503
So our group overnight pass is riding on my urine?

803
40:19.503 --> 40:21.171
- Pretty much. - Yeah.

804
40:21.171 --> 40:22.334
Isn't Barracks One quitting smoking?

805
40:22.334 --> 40:25.089
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun and Corporal Im Da Hye said

806
40:25.089 --> 40:29.552
it was too much trouble to go out, so we're doing it on our own.

807
40:29.552 --> 40:31.568
We want to go out.

808
40:32.292 --> 40:34.974
Bit Na Ri... please help us.

809
40:34.974 --> 40:37.727
- Please. - Please.

810
40:37.727 --> 40:39.125
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri. Understood!

811
40:39.125 --> 40:41.689
- Okay! - Nice!

812
40:41.689 --> 40:44.275
But I have one small favor.

813
40:44.275 --> 40:46.442
What? Name it!

814
40:52.959 --> 40:54.035
Look at you go.

815
40:54.035 --> 40:55.930
What a great appetite.

816
41:00.292 --> 41:02.083
My throat's a little dry.

817
41:02.083 --> 41:04.671
If you get dehydrated,

818
41:04.671 --> 41:09.334
your urine gets more concentrated, which makes nicotine more likely to show up.

819
41:09.334 --> 41:12.347
So could I have a cold sports drink?

820
41:12.347 --> 41:15.023
- Jeon Sekai! - Understood!

821
41:19.459 --> 41:23.083
- We don't have any. - If you don't have it, improvise!

822
41:23.083 --> 41:25.191
What about a Coke?

823
41:25.191 --> 41:27.250
I'd rather not have anything carbonated...

824
41:27.250 --> 41:29.334
- I'll go get one right now! - Yeah, go.

825
41:29.334 --> 41:30.991
Moon Bit Na Ri,

826
41:30.991 --> 41:34.075
I brought your favorite Schnell Chicken and Big Farm.

827
41:34.075 --> 41:36.876
- I got them just for you. - Thank you. Schnell Chicken!

828
41:36.876 --> 41:38.887
Eat up.

829
41:40.876 --> 41:42.792
- What? - What is it?

830
41:42.792 --> 41:44.752
- It's cold. - Cold?

831
41:44.752 --> 41:46.965
- Hey, who heated this up? - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho.

832
41:46.965 --> 41:49.000
You're a corporal and can't even heat up frozen food?

833
41:49.000 --> 41:50.675
- Sorry. - It's okay.

834
41:50.675 --> 41:51.884
It still tastes good cold.

835
41:51.884 --> 41:54.095
- Really? - I'm just a little worried...

836
41:54.095 --> 41:55.805
What if eating this cold upsets my stomach

837
41:55.805 --> 41:58.626
and affects my test results? That's what I'm worried about.

838
41:58.626 --> 42:00.500
Right.

839
42:00.500 --> 42:02.334
I'll heat it up again!

840
42:02.334 --> 42:03.521
Hurry!

841
42:03.521 --> 42:07.074
You really are fast. Must be that phys ed degree.

842
42:07.819 --> 42:10.500
- This guy's funny. - He's funny.

843
42:10.500 --> 42:12.000
Hey, buddy!

844
42:12.000 --> 42:14.907
One ice-cold sports drink, coming right up!

845
42:14.907 --> 42:16.576
My hands are freezing.

846
42:16.576 --> 42:17.829
I'll open it for you.

847
42:17.829 --> 42:19.500
Wait.

848
42:19.500 --> 42:20.705
Can I have it later?

849
42:20.705 --> 42:23.453
I don't think I should have it with all this right now.

850
42:24.419 --> 42:26.209
Sure.

851
42:26.209 --> 42:28.209
- You pig... - Are you crazy?

852
42:28.209 --> 42:29.424
- What did you say? - Nothing!

853
42:29.424 --> 42:31.149
I'll be right here. Let me know if you need anything.

854
42:31.149 --> 42:32.626
Okay.

855
42:32.626 --> 42:35.006
Now let's try the sausage.

856
42:35.834 --> 42:37.513
That's hot.

857
42:37.513 --> 42:40.143
You can't have it hot. Let me cool it down for you.

858
42:40.143 --> 42:41.728
Careful!

859
42:41.728 --> 42:44.570
Don't get any spit on it.

860
42:46.167 --> 42:48.107
I didn't know you'd all be this nice to me.

861
42:48.107 --> 42:49.672
Thank you.

862
42:56.792 --> 42:58.483
No...

863
43:00.792 --> 43:03.250
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, are you cold?

864
43:03.250 --> 43:05.413
Why are your hands shaking so much?

865
43:06.125 --> 43:07.334
No.

866
43:07.334 --> 43:10.591
I'm just so excited about going on an overnight pass.

867
43:10.591 --> 43:12.577
I'm excited too.

868
43:14.803 --> 43:16.918
- The sports drink. - Oh, right.

869
43:16.918 --> 43:18.918
Here.

870
43:18.918 --> 43:20.417
Where's the straw?

871
43:20.417 --> 43:22.266
Of course.

872
43:22.266 --> 43:23.973
Okay.

873
43:35.876 --> 43:37.000
Men.

874
43:37.000 --> 43:38.535
Have you all managed not to smoke?

875
43:38.535 --> 43:40.034
- Yes, we have. - Yes, we have.

876
43:40.034 --> 43:43.751
Good. I trust you've all been sticking to the no-smoking program.

877
43:43.751 --> 43:46.210
- We'll do a urine test. - Okay.

878
43:46.210 --> 43:49.709
I, your platoon leader, will oversee the urine test from here on out!

879
43:49.709 --> 43:52.505
- Barracks Three will go first! - Right away!

880
43:52.505 --> 43:54.417
You can start now.

881
43:54.417 --> 43:56.792
- Kang Chan Seok. - Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!

882
43:56.792 --> 43:58.427
Choi Byeong Nam.

883
43:58.427 --> 44:00.209
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

884
44:00.209 --> 44:02.390
- Kim Dong Woo. - Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

885
44:02.390 --> 44:03.959
[Choi Byeong Nam]

886
44:03.959 --> 44:05.938
Bit Na Ri, you drank plenty of water, right?

887
44:05.938 --> 44:09.584
Yes. If I relax now, I can go right away.

888
44:09.584 --> 44:12.240
- Byeong Ho, keep watch. - Got it.

889
44:24.667 --> 44:27.039
I can't go if you keep staring...

890
44:27.039 --> 44:28.375
I'm sorry.

891
44:28.375 --> 44:29.545
All right, everyone, turn around.

892
44:29.545 --> 44:30.687
- Got it. - Got it.

893
44:30.687 --> 44:32.253
Tell us when you start.

894
44:32.253 --> 44:34.172
- Got it. - You guys get ready too.

895
44:34.172 --> 44:36.192
- Got it. - Got it.

896
44:40.848 --> 44:42.015
Now!

897
44:42.015 --> 44:43.661
Hurry up.

898
44:44.751 --> 44:48.000
- It splashed on me. - That's disgusting. What are we doing?

899
44:48.000 --> 44:49.270
Right now, this is liquid gold.

900
44:49.270 --> 44:51.108
Hurry!

901
44:51.108 --> 44:53.039
Push!

902
44:54.945 --> 44:55.985
One line!

903
44:55.985 --> 44:58.292
- One line! - One line!

904
44:58.292 --> 44:59.607
I got one line too!

905
44:59.607 --> 45:01.741
- Good work, Bit Na Ri. - Thank you!

906
45:01.741 --> 45:04.785
- Hey, one line means smoke-free, right? - Yes.

907
45:04.785 --> 45:05.912
Wait...

908
45:05.912 --> 45:07.876
don't two lines mean you're smoke-free?

909
45:07.876 --> 45:09.084
What?

910
45:09.084 --> 45:10.250
What the...

911
45:10.250 --> 45:11.626
Then why'd we get one line?

912
45:11.626 --> 45:14.918
- You don't even smoke. - Huh? What is this?

913
45:14.918 --> 45:16.133
- You bastard. - Hold on.

914
45:16.133 --> 45:17.215
You smoked, didn't you?

915
45:17.215 --> 45:19.383
No. I really didn't.

916
45:19.383 --> 45:21.280
Then what is it?

917
45:22.375 --> 45:24.415
Could it be these?

918
45:26.542 --> 45:28.000
What?

919
45:28.000 --> 45:29.060
What are those?

920
45:29.060 --> 45:30.876
Nicotine patches.

921
45:30.876 --> 45:32.104
Why would you...

922
45:32.104 --> 45:33.918
I heard these would keep nicotine out

923
45:33.918 --> 45:36.400
even if people smoked around me, so I put them on.

924
45:36.400 --> 45:37.693
Man...

925
45:37.693 --> 45:38.709
Is he an idiot?

926
45:38.709 --> 45:40.947
Did he really get into Hanguk University?

927
45:40.947 --> 45:42.918
Hey, the whole point of this test

928
45:42.918 --> 45:45.292
is to see whether there's nicotine in your urine.

929
45:45.292 --> 45:46.918
If you're wearing those things,

930
45:46.918 --> 45:49.667
of course nicotine's going to show up in your urine!

931
45:49.667 --> 45:51.083
I'm sorry.

932
45:51.083 --> 45:52.709
What an idiot...

933
45:52.709 --> 45:53.793
Men!

934
45:53.793 --> 45:54.963
What's taking so long?

935
45:54.963 --> 45:56.712
The other platoons need to do this too.

936
45:56.712 --> 45:58.214
If this were a real operation,

937
45:58.214 --> 46:01.717
this delay could've gotten the entire unit wiped out...

938
46:03.918 --> 46:04.929
Platoon Leader!

939
46:04.929 --> 46:06.681
What is it, Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam?

940
46:06.681 --> 46:09.811
Judging by how happy you are to see me, you must want something.

941
46:09.811 --> 46:11.709
You don't smoke, do you, sir?

942
46:11.709 --> 46:12.728
Of course not!

943
46:12.728 --> 46:14.272
My body belongs to the nation.

944
46:14.272 --> 46:18.125
For devotion to the nation, I've never touched a cigarette in my life.

945
46:18.125 --> 46:21.125
Then please save us, sir...

946
46:21.125 --> 46:23.698
Save you? What do you mean?

947
46:23.698 --> 46:25.685
Could we have some of your urine?

948
46:26.284 --> 46:28.794
- My urine? - Yes, sir. Your urine.

949
46:30.204 --> 46:36.827
You want my non-smoking urine for the nicotine test...

950
46:37.420 --> 46:39.505
don't you?

951
46:39.505 --> 46:42.000
I'm afraid I can't do that. It would be unethical.

952
46:42.000 --> 46:44.417
Platoon Leader...

953
46:44.417 --> 46:46.804
Please.

954
46:46.804 --> 46:51.767
We desperately want to go on an overnight pass with Sergeant Kang Chan Seok

955
46:51.767 --> 46:53.792
and Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam before they get discharged.

956
46:53.792 --> 46:55.774
It's what all of us want.

957
46:55.774 --> 47:00.276
Couldn't you make that happen for us, sir?

958
47:00.276 --> 47:03.286
- Please. - Please.

959
47:04.741 --> 47:06.487
I cannot!

960
47:07.626 --> 47:09.660
I really believed in you, sir...

961
47:09.660 --> 47:10.828
I really did...

962
47:10.828 --> 47:15.291
I believe a soldier's morale comes from trust.

963
47:15.291 --> 47:17.209
Once that trust is broken,

964
47:17.209 --> 47:19.547
combat effectiveness collapses.

965
47:21.464 --> 47:23.341
Wait, men!

966
47:23.341 --> 47:24.842
Do you trust your platoon leader?

967
47:24.842 --> 47:26.597
- We do. - We trust you.

968
47:26.597 --> 47:29.417
I'll ask again. Do you trust your platoon leader?

969
47:29.417 --> 47:30.459
- We trust you! - We trust you!

970
47:30.459 --> 47:32.399
Are you saying I'm a commander...

971
47:33.392 --> 47:34.751
you can count on?

972
47:34.751 --> 47:36.789
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

973
47:39.334 --> 47:41.442
Platoon Leader!

974
47:41.442 --> 47:43.414
- Platoon Leader. - Platoon Leader.

975
47:44.862 --> 47:45.863
Platoon Leader.

976
47:45.863 --> 47:47.626
- We love you. - I'm moved.

977
47:47.626 --> 47:49.116
Just a little more.

978
47:49.116 --> 47:50.871
A little more.

979
47:50.871 --> 47:52.836
Just a little more.

980
47:54.042 --> 47:56.691
That hurts.

981
47:57.666 --> 48:00.547
We're running out of time.

982
48:01.465 --> 48:02.959
Should you drink some more water?

983
48:02.959 --> 48:04.546
I'm fine.

984
48:06.834 --> 48:09.056
One, two, three... six.

985
48:09.056 --> 48:10.792
Not yet.

986
48:10.792 --> 48:12.125
We have to do this now.

987
48:12.125 --> 48:13.753
We're...

988
48:15.187 --> 48:17.215
- It's time. - Hey.

989
48:17.215 --> 48:18.357
Line up by rank.

990
48:18.357 --> 48:19.542
Keep it orderly.

991
48:19.542 --> 48:21.610
Yes, sir.

992
48:21.610 --> 48:22.650
Go.

993
48:22.650 --> 48:23.791
Excuse me.

994
48:23.791 --> 48:25.209
- Next. - It's an honor, sir.

995
48:25.209 --> 48:26.417
Next.

996
48:26.417 --> 48:27.626
- I'll do my best. - Next.

997
48:27.626 --> 48:29.250
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min. - Next.

998
48:29.250 --> 48:30.241
Hold.

999
48:30.241 --> 48:31.700
Platoon Leader, what's wrong?

1000
48:31.700 --> 48:32.993
I'm almost out.

1001
48:32.993 --> 48:34.620
- Hurry. - Two men left.

1002
48:34.620 --> 48:35.996
- Go. - Go.

1003
48:35.996 --> 48:37.123
Thank you.

1004
48:37.123 --> 48:39.834
Private Jeon Se Gye. Thank you, sir.

1005
48:39.834 --> 48:40.959
Hold on.

1006
48:40.959 --> 48:42.086
Didn't you already get some?

1007
48:42.086 --> 48:43.337
I'm doing a double-check, sir.

1008
48:43.337 --> 48:44.922
Double-check, okay. Next.

1009
48:44.922 --> 48:46.715
Better safe than sorry.

1010
48:46.715 --> 48:48.384
- Till the end! - Five!

1011
48:48.384 --> 48:49.635
- One more time. - Four!

1012
48:49.635 --> 48:52.167
- I'm the last one. - Three, two...

1013
48:52.167 --> 48:53.995
one...

1014
48:55.334 --> 48:56.751
Two lines.

1015
48:56.751 --> 48:58.167
Two lines.

1016
48:58.167 --> 49:01.918
- Two lines! - Two lines!

1017
49:01.918 --> 49:04.167
Platoon, attention.

1018
49:04.167 --> 49:07.361
Salute our platoon leader, full of passion and spirit.

1019
49:07.361 --> 49:10.038
- Chungseong. Love you. - Chungseong. Love you.

1020
49:11.375 --> 49:14.702
Chungseong. Love you too.

1021
49:14.702 --> 49:18.652
What happened today stays a secret within this platoon forever. Understood?

1022
49:18.652 --> 49:20.563
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

1023
49:24.667 --> 49:26.508
- Nice work. - Thank you.

1024
49:26.508 --> 49:31.775
- Overnight pass. - Overnight pass.

1025
49:35.225 --> 49:37.308
Man... today was rough.

1026
49:37.308 --> 49:38.478
Thank you for your hard work.

1027
49:38.478 --> 49:39.518
Thank you for your hard work.

1028
49:39.518 --> 49:42.357
Nice work today. You all did well.

1029
49:42.357 --> 49:44.709
Take care of your stuff for now,

1030
49:44.709 --> 49:46.734
and when it's time, let's go eat. I'm hungry too.

1031
49:46.734 --> 49:48.652
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

1032
49:48.652 --> 49:50.279
Hey, Park Min Seok. You're not answering?

1033
49:50.279 --> 49:53.125
What's been wrong with you all day?

1034
49:53.125 --> 49:56.042
No, sir. I'm fine.

1035
49:56.042 --> 50:00.414
Why have you been hanging around here all day?

1036
50:00.414 --> 50:03.308
What am I doing at the officers' quarters? I'll just get dragged out drinking again.

1037
50:03.308 --> 50:06.504
All this drinking is killing me.

1038
50:06.504 --> 50:07.963
I'm more comfortable here.

1039
50:07.963 --> 50:09.292
Wake me when it's time.

1040
50:09.292 --> 50:10.802
Yes, sir.

1041
50:10.802 --> 50:12.218
Hyeon Uk.

1042
50:12.218 --> 50:13.552
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1043
50:13.552 --> 50:14.803
- Grab your boots. - Yes.

1044
50:14.803 --> 50:16.950
- I'll come too. - Okay.

1045
50:22.918 --> 50:24.522
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu...

1046
50:24.522 --> 50:26.209
Yeah, what?

1047
50:26.209 --> 50:28.734
Do you have a minute?

1048
50:28.734 --> 50:31.323
A minute? Nope.

1049
50:31.323 --> 50:32.794
Oh, come on.

1050
50:32.794 --> 50:35.994
Why are you getting all serious on me?

1051
50:35.994 --> 50:37.645
Can we talk for a second?

1052
50:37.645 --> 50:39.905
What a pain...

1053
50:41.250 --> 50:42.873
Fine. Let's go.

1054
50:42.873 --> 50:45.267
You've been acting weird today.

1055
50:51.176 --> 50:53.425
What is it?

1056
50:53.425 --> 50:56.595
There's something I wanted to ask you.

1057
50:56.595 --> 50:57.808
What?

1058
50:57.808 --> 51:00.391
Going to be a noncommissioned officer? Is that what's bothering you?

1059
51:00.391 --> 51:02.125
No, it's not that.

1060
51:02.125 --> 51:04.053
Then what?

1061
51:04.770 --> 51:07.439
Someone has the wrong idea about me,

1062
51:07.439 --> 51:09.108
and I want to clear it up,

1063
51:09.108 --> 51:12.751
but I don't know how.

1064
51:12.751 --> 51:14.555
A misunderstanding...

1065
51:15.781 --> 51:18.325
I had the wrong idea about you when we first met.

1066
51:18.325 --> 51:20.581
You had glasses on, so I thought you were smart.

1067
51:20.581 --> 51:23.163
Then we talked for a few minutes,

1068
51:23.163 --> 51:28.714
and I realized right away I'd been wrong.

1069
51:28.714 --> 51:31.626
I'm really not in the mood for jokes.

1070
51:31.626 --> 51:32.918
I'm not joking.

1071
51:32.918 --> 51:34.250
Don't lie to me.

1072
51:34.250 --> 51:35.751
I'm not lying.

1073
51:35.751 --> 51:37.389
Come on...

1074
51:37.389 --> 51:39.993
Huh? Look at that face.

1075
51:42.918 --> 51:47.605
Do only you think it's a misunderstanding?

1076
51:47.605 --> 51:51.567
Or does the other person see it that way too?

1077
51:51.567 --> 51:55.279
What do you mean, whether they think it's a misunderstanding too?

1078
51:55.279 --> 51:57.239
You know.

1079
51:57.239 --> 51:59.408
Maybe you think it's a misunderstanding,

1080
51:59.408 --> 52:03.287
but they think you actually did something wrong.

1081
52:03.287 --> 52:06.204
Oh. Yes. Exactly. That's exactly it.

1082
52:06.204 --> 52:08.417
I just told you.

1083
52:08.417 --> 52:09.838
I had the wrong idea about you,

1084
52:09.838 --> 52:13.119
but after talking to you for a few minutes, I realized I'd misunderstood you.

1085
52:17.179 --> 52:18.972
There's a saying.

1086
52:18.972 --> 52:22.097
Misunderstandings grow in silence

1087
52:22.097 --> 52:24.608
and disappear through conversation.

1088
52:26.522 --> 52:28.820
That actually sounds pretty cool.

1089
52:29.584 --> 52:33.042
I've always been cool.

1090
52:33.042 --> 52:34.978
Yes.

1091
52:37.324 --> 52:39.615
Thank you.

1092
52:39.615 --> 52:42.000
What are you thanking me for?

1093
52:56.009 --> 52:58.209
Man, I want to go home.

1094
52:58.209 --> 52:59.346
Don't you?

1095
52:59.346 --> 53:00.886
Yes.

1096
53:00.886 --> 53:02.327
Already?

1097
53:02.959 --> 53:04.470
I'm sorry.

1098
53:05.709 --> 53:08.769
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1099
53:08.769 --> 53:10.042
Are you settling in okay?

1100
53:10.042 --> 53:11.438
Yes. I love it here.

1101
53:11.438 --> 53:15.492
- Have you taken your special leave yet? - Not yet.

1102
53:16.151 --> 53:18.119
You want to get out of here soon, right?

1103
53:18.737 --> 53:19.947
Yes.

1104
53:19.947 --> 53:21.490
What's the first thing you want to do?

1105
53:21.490 --> 53:23.534
Nothing special.

1106
53:23.534 --> 53:26.453
I want to have a few drinks with my friends.

1107
53:26.453 --> 53:28.000
And more than anything,

1108
53:28.000 --> 53:30.210
- I just want to sleep as long as I want. - Right.

1109
53:30.210 --> 53:33.755
Nothing beats getting drunk and sleeping in on leave. Right?

1110
53:33.755 --> 53:34.795
Yes.

1111
53:34.795 --> 53:36.884
How are the guys? Are they treating you well?

1112
53:36.884 --> 53:38.218
Everyone's been great to me.

1113
53:38.218 --> 53:41.388
Yeah, well, it's Barracks One. Everyone there is pretty good.

1114
53:41.388 --> 53:42.553
Yes.

1115
53:42.553 --> 53:45.055
Im Da Hye, how about him? Isn't he a year ahead of you?

1116
53:45.055 --> 53:46.849
Yes.

1117
53:46.849 --> 53:49.810
Does he go, "Son?"

1118
53:49.810 --> 53:51.500
- Huh? - That's exactly how he sounds!

1119
53:51.500 --> 53:53.015
Really?

1120
53:58.918 --> 54:00.487
Oh, right.

1121
54:00.487 --> 54:03.289
You and Min Seok really went through boot camp together?

1122
54:04.459 --> 54:06.201
Yes.

1123
54:06.201 --> 54:08.495
That's pretty wild.

1124
54:08.495 --> 54:10.497
Yes.

1125
54:10.497 --> 54:12.166
Does Min Seok treat you well?

1126
54:12.166 --> 54:13.882
Yes.

1127
54:15.839 --> 54:17.337
Kind of crazy, isn't it?

1128
54:17.337 --> 54:19.173
Being the Division Commander's son?

1129
54:19.173 --> 54:22.259
Yes. I've never met one before.

1130
54:22.259 --> 54:26.426
He could've had a cushy assignment at first, but he turned it down.

1131
54:27.681 --> 54:29.311
I...

1132
54:29.311 --> 54:31.185
don't want to go.

1133
54:31.185 --> 54:32.500
What are you talking about?

1134
54:32.500 --> 54:34.584
I'm not telling you to go. Your father is...

1135
54:34.584 --> 54:36.940
I know, sir.

1136
54:36.940 --> 54:40.426
That's exactly why I don't want to go.

1137
54:41.069 --> 54:45.574
I'm still scared and want to run away,

1138
54:45.574 --> 54:48.076
but I want to see this through.

1139
54:48.076 --> 54:49.786
You said you wouldn't go?

1140
54:49.786 --> 54:52.372
Yes.

1141
54:52.372 --> 54:55.167
He made things awkward for everybody.

1142
54:55.167 --> 54:56.667
And get this.

1143
54:56.667 --> 54:58.962
He's never taken a single reward leave.

1144
54:58.962 --> 55:00.801
Not once?

1145
55:00.801 --> 55:02.216
No.

1146
55:02.216 --> 55:03.792
Seriously...

1147
55:03.792 --> 55:06.804
If it were me, I'd be asking for leave every chance I got.

1148
55:06.804 --> 55:10.265
So I asked him why he kept turning down the leave everyone else takes

1149
55:10.265 --> 55:12.688
and letting other guys have it.

1150
55:12.688 --> 55:15.542
And Min Seok said...

1151
55:15.542 --> 55:16.855
Well...

1152
55:16.855 --> 55:18.982
Because my father's the Division Commander,

1153
55:18.982 --> 55:20.609
I was afraid people would say

1154
55:20.609 --> 55:23.070
I only got it because of him, even if I earned it myself.

1155
55:23.070 --> 55:26.098
So I turned down every reward leave.

1156
55:27.449 --> 55:29.868
That made me think, I guess I can see why.

1157
55:29.868 --> 55:34.206
You know how kids of sports stars are expected to be good at everything?

1158
55:34.206 --> 55:38.460
Maybe Min Seok feels that kind of pressure too.

1159
55:38.460 --> 55:41.046
He never flaunts being the Division Commander's son.

1160
55:41.046 --> 55:45.300
I bet he would've kept it secret

1161
55:45.300 --> 55:48.512
if everyone hadn't made such a big deal out of it.

1162
55:48.512 --> 55:51.038
- Really? - Yeah.

1163
55:54.000 --> 55:57.187
Hyeon Uk... I really didn't know.

1164
55:57.187 --> 55:59.648
I didn't know you were such an asshole either.

1165
55:59.648 --> 56:01.570
You acted like you weren't the Division Commander's son

1166
56:01.570 --> 56:03.746
but still took every perk that came with it.

1167
56:04.862 --> 56:08.907
I can still see you getting into that ambulance just to save your own skin.

1168
56:08.907 --> 56:11.159
No, that's not what happened.

1169
56:11.159 --> 56:14.250
I really didn't know you were hurt that badly then.

1170
56:14.250 --> 56:18.333
You can just say you didn't know, and that makes everything okay, right?

1171
56:18.333 --> 56:21.920
The army made me sick back then.

1172
56:21.920 --> 56:23.839
Now it makes me even sicker.

1173
56:23.839 --> 56:26.258
I wanted to see how far they'd go to cover for you.

1174
56:26.258 --> 56:28.010
Turns out nothing's changed.

1175
56:28.010 --> 56:30.262
I think what happened yesterday

1176
56:30.262 --> 56:32.542
was the kind of mistake anyone could make...

1177
56:32.542 --> 56:34.308
You make a mistake, they let it slide.

1178
56:34.308 --> 56:36.018
You fire a blank, they let it slide.

1179
56:36.018 --> 56:39.107
You lose the firing pin retaining pin, they let it slide.

1180
56:39.107 --> 56:42.222
No. That's really not what happened.

1181
56:44.484 --> 56:47.679
Now you get to feel it too.

1182
56:47.679 --> 56:48.780
See how far I'll go.

1183
56:48.780 --> 56:52.436
And how far this place will go to protect you.

1184
57:02.002 --> 57:03.946
Knowing Corporal Park Min Seok...

1185
57:05.172 --> 57:07.299
I could see that.

1186
57:12.125 --> 57:13.584
Hey, someone's coming.

1187
57:13.584 --> 57:16.144
Just kidding.

1188
57:16.144 --> 57:17.851
Hey, are you laughing?

1189
57:17.851 --> 57:19.331
I'm sorry.

1190
57:20.918 --> 57:22.738
Cheers!

1191
57:26.238 --> 57:30.042
Who am I going to drink with if you leave?

1192
57:30.042 --> 57:31.994
Why are you saying goodbye already?

1193
57:31.994 --> 57:33.292
The results aren't even out yet.

1194
57:33.292 --> 57:37.583
You should've just kept your head down. Why'd you have to make such a scene?

1195
57:37.583 --> 57:40.540
If I don't get promoted, at least I'll have something to blame it on.

1196
57:40.540 --> 57:43.083
That actually takes some pressure off.

1197
57:43.083 --> 57:45.420
You really are a strange one.

1198
57:45.420 --> 57:49.265
Maybe all the oddballs end up in our unit.

1199
57:50.092 --> 57:53.303
Maybe that's why you're here too.

1200
57:53.303 --> 57:55.396
Can't argue with that.

1201
58:00.230 --> 58:02.657
Think the kid's doing okay?

1202
58:03.397 --> 58:08.068
I put Il Gu, Dong Woo, and a few of the guys with him,

1203
58:08.068 --> 58:11.405
but I don't know if it'll help.

1204
58:11.405 --> 58:13.240
Annoyed I called you in this early?

1205
58:13.240 --> 58:14.866
No, sir.

1206
58:14.866 --> 58:16.660
It's nice seeing you this early.

1207
58:16.660 --> 58:18.498
Don't give me that. It's written all over your face.

1208
58:18.498 --> 58:22.667
No. My eyes are just puffy in the morning.

1209
58:22.667 --> 58:25.502
What did you need me for this early?

1210
58:25.502 --> 58:28.626
Can you stick close to Min Seok today?

1211
58:28.626 --> 58:30.966
Is something going on with Min Seok?

1212
58:30.966 --> 58:33.263
I know it's a hassle, but I need you to pull guard duty.

1213
58:33.263 --> 58:34.428
Yes, sir.

1214
58:34.428 --> 58:37.897
In return, the late-night snack's on me.

1215
58:41.101 --> 58:45.564
I'm even throwing in tuna, so make this mission a success.

1216
58:45.564 --> 58:47.167
Yes, sir.

1217
58:47.167 --> 58:49.484
I hope it works out.

1218
58:49.484 --> 58:51.862
I can't help worrying as their Company Commander.

1219
58:51.862 --> 58:54.042
Forget about them.

1220
58:54.042 --> 58:56.251
Worry about yourself.

1221
58:57.242 --> 58:58.952
The men come first for me.

1222
58:58.952 --> 59:02.042
You're one of the guys I look after too.

1223
59:02.042 --> 59:05.295
Then I'll look after the men,

1224
59:05.295 --> 59:07.669
and you look after me.

1225
59:07.669 --> 59:09.500
Should I?

1226
59:09.500 --> 59:12.799
Yeah. And while you're at it,

1227
59:12.799 --> 59:15.142
take care of this check too.

1228
59:18.889 --> 59:21.933
- Oh, but what are we going to do? - Why?

1229
59:21.933 --> 59:24.811
- I'm taking care of you... - Right.

1230
59:24.811 --> 59:27.314
- And taking care of this check... - Right.

1231
59:27.314 --> 59:30.283
But I forgot to bring my card.

1232
59:36.493 --> 59:38.375
Then let's split it.

1233
59:38.375 --> 59:39.659
Shall we?

1234
59:39.659 --> 59:41.832
You just said you didn't bring your card.

1235
59:41.832 --> 59:43.609
What do we do now?

1236
59:45.626 --> 59:48.167
At this rate, you'll own a whole building someday.

1237
59:48.167 --> 59:50.883
- A building? - You're unbelievable.

1238
59:50.883 --> 59:52.217
I'm going to the restroom.

1239
59:52.217 --> 59:53.882
- Freeze! - No.

1240
59:53.882 --> 59:56.542
- Where are you going? - I'm really going to the restroom.

1241
59:56.542 --> 59:59.141
What am I going to do?

1242
59:59.141 --> 01:00:00.914
What should I do...

1243
01:00:20.500 --> 01:00:25.083
What Corporal Kim Dong Woo told me back then

1244
01:00:25.083 --> 01:00:27.657
really helped me.

1245
01:00:28.337 --> 01:00:30.836
He said...

1246
01:00:30.836 --> 01:00:33.721
If you ask for forgiveness

1247
01:00:34.798 --> 01:00:37.721
and truly mean it,

1248
01:00:37.721 --> 01:00:41.983
one day, the other person will understand that.

1249
01:00:42.889 --> 01:00:45.921
You won't know when that day will come,

1250
01:00:46.542 --> 01:00:47.561
but...

1251
01:00:47.561 --> 01:00:51.398
But forgiving someone is never easy.

1252
01:00:51.398 --> 01:00:52.566
That's true.

1253
01:00:52.566 --> 01:00:56.236
Of course, it takes courage to ask for forgiveness,

1254
01:00:56.236 --> 01:00:58.655
but accepting that apology...

1255
01:00:58.655 --> 01:01:01.456
He said that takes even more courage.

1256
01:01:03.205 --> 01:01:08.123
I was nodding like crazy when he said that.

1257
01:01:08.123 --> 01:01:11.199
Corporal Kim Dong Woo is seriously cool.

1258
01:01:13.131 --> 01:01:15.338
I wish I could be that kind of leader.

1259
01:01:15.338 --> 01:01:19.033
You're a good leader too.

1260
01:01:19.634 --> 01:01:21.682
- Really? - There are...

1261
01:01:21.682 --> 01:01:25.167
different kinds of good leaders, aren't there?

1262
01:01:25.167 --> 01:01:27.521
Well, I guess...

1263
01:01:27.521 --> 01:01:30.770
That compliment gives me a lot to think about.

1264
01:01:30.770 --> 01:01:31.918
No.

1265
01:01:31.918 --> 01:01:36.218
The guys under you really do all like you.

1266
01:01:37.277 --> 01:01:39.321
Not all of them...

1267
01:01:39.321 --> 01:01:41.635
I really wish they did.

1268
01:01:47.120 --> 01:01:48.496
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1269
01:01:48.496 --> 01:01:50.209
Why aren't you inside?

1270
01:01:50.209 --> 01:01:52.083
I was waiting for you.

1271
01:01:52.083 --> 01:01:54.077
I told you to wait inside.

1272
01:01:56.250 --> 01:01:59.052
What are you two doing? On a date?

1273
01:01:59.052 --> 01:02:00.467
Speak of the devil.

1274
01:02:00.467 --> 01:02:01.468
What?

1275
01:02:01.468 --> 01:02:04.516
We were just talking about you.

1276
01:02:04.516 --> 01:02:07.235
- He was talking trash about me, right? - That's right.

1277
01:02:07.235 --> 01:02:09.643
No. Of course not.

1278
01:02:09.643 --> 01:02:12.517
[Building an Advanced Barracks Culture Together]

1279
01:02:32.252 --> 01:02:35.168
Special treatment isn't always a good thing.

1280
01:02:35.168 --> 01:02:36.586
It can make things uncomfortable.

1281
01:02:36.586 --> 01:02:38.334
Especially when you don't even want it.

1282
01:02:38.334 --> 01:02:39.756
Corporal Park Min Seok!

1283
01:02:39.756 --> 01:02:41.383
With such an outstanding father,

1284
01:02:41.383 --> 01:02:44.556
I'm sure you'll be an outstanding soldier too.

1285
01:02:44.556 --> 01:02:45.933
Must be nice.

1286
01:02:45.933 --> 01:02:48.942
Nothing beats being born into the right military family, huh?

1287
01:02:48.942 --> 01:02:51.159
Being the Division Commander's son sure has its perks.

1288
01:02:51.159 --> 01:02:52.231
They just let it slide.

1289
01:02:52.231 --> 01:02:54.483
That's not what happened.

1290
01:02:54.483 --> 01:02:56.273
Sorry...

1291
01:02:56.273 --> 01:02:58.028
I'm sorry...

1292
01:02:58.028 --> 01:03:02.582
You know how kids of sports stars are expected to be good at everything?

1293
01:03:04.201 --> 01:03:06.825
Man, it's hot.

1294
01:03:06.825 --> 01:03:10.736
- Min Seok, you're doing great. Hurry up. - Thank you.

1295
01:03:10.736 --> 01:03:15.040
Maybe Min Seok feels that kind of pressure too.

1296
01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:17.584
Sorry...

1297
01:03:17.584 --> 01:03:19.501
I'm sorry...

1298
01:03:31.667 --> 01:03:33.442
Yeah, come in.

1299
01:03:38.193 --> 01:03:39.858
Chungseong! Love you!

1300
01:03:39.858 --> 01:03:42.819
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo, reporting to the Company Commander's office.

1301
01:03:42.819 --> 01:03:46.205
- I'm here to deliver the Defense Daily. - To deliver the Defense Daily.

1302
01:03:47.115 --> 01:03:49.121
Yes, sir. That's right.

1303
01:03:49.121 --> 01:03:50.535
All right. Appreciate the hard work.

1304
01:03:50.535 --> 01:03:52.636
- Thank you, sir. - Yeah.

1305
01:03:53.667 --> 01:03:57.042
The Battalion Commander is in the paper again today.

1306
01:03:57.042 --> 01:03:59.335
Again? He's in there all the time.

1307
01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:00.959
Yes, sir.

1308
01:04:00.959 --> 01:04:03.006
Then I'll be going.

1309
01:04:03.006 --> 01:04:04.292
Chungseong! Love you!

1310
01:04:04.292 --> 01:04:06.134
Yeah. Love you too.

1311
01:04:06.134 --> 01:04:09.144
- Yes, sir. Take care. - Yeah. Careful.

1312
01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:11.511
[Defense Daily]

1313
01:04:19.856 --> 01:04:23.103
He sure photographs well.

1314
01:04:24.069 --> 01:04:25.862
"An elite battalion built on love..."

1315
01:04:25.862 --> 01:04:27.947
"Leading a new culture of communication in the barracks..."

1316
01:04:27.947 --> 01:04:30.033
That's a good headline.

1317
01:04:33.119 --> 01:04:35.918
"Shinhwa Unit commander Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin introduced

1318
01:04:35.918 --> 01:04:39.042
the unconventional salute 'Chungseong! Love you!' upon taking command..."

1319
01:04:39.042 --> 01:04:40.877
From now on, Second Company's salute

1320
01:04:40.877 --> 01:04:43.091
will be "Chungseong! Love you!"

1321
01:04:43.091 --> 01:04:45.751
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

1322
01:04:45.751 --> 01:04:49.219
"The 'singing roll call,' introduced after hours to relieve stress

1323
01:04:49.219 --> 01:04:53.348
and boost morale, also helped foster a culture of communication in the barracks.

1324
01:04:53.348 --> 01:04:56.626
It was another innovative idea by Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin.

1325
01:04:56.626 --> 01:04:59.650
To help newly arrived recruits relax,

1326
01:04:59.650 --> 01:05:01.773
he personally took them to a public bathhouse

1327
01:05:01.773 --> 01:05:07.112
and even scrubbed the soldiers' backs, an unconventional show of leadership."

1328
01:05:07.112 --> 01:05:08.125
Good to see you.

1329
01:05:08.125 --> 01:05:09.751
It's been a while, Battalion Commander.

1330
01:05:09.751 --> 01:05:11.743
He's a reporter from Defense Daily.

1331
01:05:16.166 --> 01:05:17.914
What is this?

1332
01:05:17.914 --> 01:05:19.305
[Battalion commander Byeon Hyeok Jin]

1333
01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:23.560
[Battalion commander Byeon Hyeok Jin]

1334
01:05:26.792 --> 01:05:29.134
Yes, sir. This is the Second Company Commander.

1335
01:05:29.134 --> 01:05:31.359
Can we talk for a minute?
